        rules: {
          objective: 'Collect and hold an uninterrupted sequence of the highest trump cards.',
          gameplay: "Matadors are usually the cards that can lead a trick and force opponents to play their own trumps, effectively 'clearing' the table.",
          keyRules: [
            'Matadors are the highest trumps in an uninterrupted sequence (e.g. consecutive Jacks in Skat).',
            'Matadors can lead a trick and force opponents to play trumps, clearing the table.',
            'In Skat, matadors are Jacks only; in Ombre they include Spadille, Manille, and Basto.',
            'Payment or scoring bonuses apply for matadors held or lost; the multiplier affects game value.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: "Identify your 'Chain'. If you are missing the highest Matador (e.g., you have 3 Jacks but not the Clubs), you are 'Against 1'. This significantly changes how you bid.",
          intermediate: "The Lead Trap: If you hold several Matadors, lead them consecutively. This consumes your opponents' trumps while you maintain the lead, eventually leaving your middle-cards as the highest on the table.",
          advanced: "Bidding Risk: Bid high when you have many Matadors, as the multiplier ensures a massive score. However, if you are 'Against' many Matadors, your point-capture must be near perfect to win.",
          tips: [
            "In Skat, 'Matadors' are only Jacks. In Ombre, they include the Ace of Spades and certain low cards of the trump suit.",
            "Always check the specific 'Matador' list for the game variant you are playing.",
